WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.740
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.390
- Have you ever met Jenna, Sam,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:04.830
I don't know if anybody's ever met.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.140
- No, I haven't.
- Okay, say hi.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.340
I'm bringing people together.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.413
- Very nice to meet you.
- Hi.

00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:12.960
- Yeah, I have to admit longtime fan.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:13.793
- Oh of me?

00:00:13.793 --> 00:00:14.670
- So excited to be sitting here

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.503
with you.
- Oh.

00:00:15.503 --> 00:00:17.580
- A little nervous.
- Oh I have to admit,

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.830
I always love when people
that work out all the time

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.680
use my music to work out and I don't,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.250
(group laughing)

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.210
That's my favorite part.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.830
They're like, oh, we use you
in our class all the time,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.181
I was like, I wouldn't know.

00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:28.014
(all laughs)

00:00:28.014 --> 00:00:30.240
But I love that, thank you,
that's such a compliment

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.073
and I love your hair,

00:00:31.073 --> 00:00:32.100
I'm complimenting that as well.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.660
'Cause it's same.
- Yeah, it's so cute.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.869
- Oh, so cute.
- You would look cute.

00:00:34.869 --> 00:00:36.619
- Anyway, I know.

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:38.760
- Have you, I feel like
you're one of those people,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.530
you set a goal and you kill it every time,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:41.363
are you one of those people

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:42.990
that ever breaks your resolution?

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:45.240
- I generally do.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.730
I have to admit, when it comes to health,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.410
that is my job, I'm good at it.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.700
- Yeah.
- But I make resolutions

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.040
outside of health and then
I fail every single time,

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:54.339
'cause that's why it's my resolution

00:00:54.339 --> 00:00:55.172
- That makes me feel good.

00:00:55.172 --> 00:00:56.730
- 'Cause I can't do it.
- Yeah.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.580
- So like, I have tried to quit swearing.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.810
- Oh.
- For two decades.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:01.797
- Why?

00:01:01.797 --> 00:01:02.850
(group laughing)

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:04.560
- Good, that's exactly
why I gave up on it.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:05.550
- I mean, my mom will actually yeah,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.410
she tells me it's trashy,
but like, whatever.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.460
- So is my wife, she's like,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.440
you just literally, you sound so trashy,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.816
you would sound so much more-

00:01:11.816 --> 00:01:14.220
- But doesn't it feel good?
- It feels amazing.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.110
- And you can swear intelligently.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.096
- That's what,

00:01:17.096 --> 00:01:18.424
thank you.
- For Sure.

00:01:18.424 --> 00:01:19.257
- Thank you so much.

00:01:19.257 --> 00:01:20.520
In fact, there's a study that came out.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.353
- What is it?
- What's that?

00:01:21.353 --> 00:01:22.560
- Intelligent people swear

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.300
so now I just hang my hat on

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.974
like I'm exceptionally intelligent.

00:01:25.974 --> 00:01:26.936
(audience applause)

00:01:26.936 --> 00:01:27.936
- Thank you.

00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:31.170
- I just tried to narrow
it down to time and place,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.150
like, I won't drop the
F-bomb here on your show.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.470
- Okay.
- Probably on my way

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.730
to the car I'll find a reason.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.830
- Reason, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.300
- It's all right, I like it.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.370
But so for anyone wanting to make changes,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.260
it's hard, it's hard to stick with it,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.742
I think or I've been
told, with discipline.

00:01:45.742 --> 00:01:46.575
(all laughs)

00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:48.390
So how do you sustain it?

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.350
Like for the long haul?

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.183
- Yeah.
- 'Cause it's really

00:01:50.183 --> 00:01:51.150
a life choice.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.280
I feel like a lot of us will be like,

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.150
I just wanna do this,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.320
let's see if I can do it for three months,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.384
but it's really a life decision right?

00:01:57.384 --> 00:02:00.090
- So, I wanna get a little
bit more serious on you now,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.480
and try to address two
different kinds of people.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.100
The first one is the one that

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.870
the type of person that
has been approaching me

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.040
for the last several weeks,

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.280
the one that's like, ugh, I gained weight,

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.980
oh, I need to look a girl,
I need to lose 30 pounds,

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.630
and I'm like, stop.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.930
And by the way, the years have
not been kind as we all know,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.450
and it comes from the place
of like beating yourself up,

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.310
feeling disappointed with yourself.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.460
And that's the self-loathing
thing nobody wants, right?

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.800
But then the antidote to that

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.840
is the nah, girl, you're good.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.280
And the truth of the matter is,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.800
when you get into that conversation,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.590
you rob yourself of all
of this excellent growth

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.423
that you can make a-

00:02:38.423 --> 00:02:39.445
- Potential of it.
- In any facet

00:02:39.445 --> 00:02:40.560
of your life, right?

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.350
We wanna evolve, grow,
whether it's mental health,

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.540
physical health, relationships, career.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.027
- All of the above what?

00:02:47.027 --> 00:02:50.880
- All of you at inception
come from a place

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.130
of wanting to be healthy
because you love your body

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.080
not because you hate it.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:55.913
- [Molly] Yeah.

00:02:55.913 --> 00:02:59.520
- And when you begin a
journey with that intention,

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.310
the next step is to
really identify your why.

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.680
So far greater minds than me have said,

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.620
if you have a why, you
can tolerate the how.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.590
Work with purpose becomes passion,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.320
work without it is gonna feel punishing.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.290
So you better outline
like, why am I doing this?

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.340
- Yeah.
- Is this a change

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.720
I really care about?

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.570
How will my life be better?

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.310
And I don't mean I wanna be healthy,

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.210
that means nothing to me.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.200
I don't even know what that means,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.660
it's, I'm getting married this summer,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.660
and I want to feel my strongest,
most fit, healthiest best.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:33.240
I wanna live to meet
my great-grandchildren,

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.130
I lost my mother to breast cancer

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.500
and I wanna live my
healthiest life in her honor

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.030
and raise money by running a marathon,

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.680
I don't care what it is.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:41.610
- What your motivator.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.850
- As long as it does motivate you.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.770
And from that place

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:51.770
it helps you stay motivated
and make the healthier choice.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.810
And then of course small changes

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.280
are generally best for people

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.680
because they're more accessible
and more sustainable.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.060
- Attainable, yeah.
- And less overwhelming.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.140
- Yeah, less overwhelming,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.720
yeah, well, The Fitness
App by Jillian Michaels

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.690
is available for download
wherever you get your apps people.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.970
Also be sure to check
out Jillian's podcast,

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.110
Keeping It Real.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.710
I love keeping real, that's all.

